{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/909071-exotic-airs-merit","id":909071,"title":"Exotic Airs Merit","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Changeling: The Lost"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-06-07T05:41:39-07:00","id":909071,"title":"Exotic Airs Merit","content":"I noticed the Exotic Airs Merit in the glamour harevesting section of the playtest doc, and I'm guessing its like Unnatural Affinity Merit for Vampires.<br /> <br /> In other words it allows you to feed from other Supernatural types like Mages, Vampires, Werewolves, Demons, Ghosts, Spirits, Zombies, and stranger things like Strix, Supernal Entities, Goetics, Beasts, ect...<br /> <br /> In practice I don't know how much of an advantage this is when humans are plentiful enough to feed from.<br /> <br /> It might be good for Gravewrights who deal with Ghosts and to a lesser extent other empheral enitities, but how much would this come up and be an advantage outside of gravewrights?<br /> <br /> Also Exotic Airs would be cool for a Cambion Character, twisting their ability to steal glamour from Fae, to draining say vitae from vampires, or Mnna from Mages and converting it to Glamour.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-07T05:44:30-07:00","id":909074,"title":"","content":"Presumably it'll also allow you to reap those supernatural types, which is situationally awesome.<br /> <br /> Cambions are NPC characters so you can just have them do that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1157-soulgambit","name":"SoulGambit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"912"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-07T06:47:47-07:00","id":909116,"title":"","content":"Reaping a Hunter in particular is a nightmare for the Hunter as they rely heavily on Willpower. Reap a member of the Lucifuge for example and he has no willpower to use his endowments with for example.<br /> <br /> Of course tier 1 and tier 2 and some tier 3 Hunters are completely human, so they can already be reaped.<br /> <br /> The same is true for Horrors from the CoD.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-07T11:35:29-07:00","id":909324,"title":"","content":"Hunters can be reaped without a merit. They are human.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1157-soulgambit","name":"SoulGambit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"912"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-07T14:41:27-07:00","id":909501,"title":"","content":"I'm not sure the Lucifuge are entirely human?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-07T15:42:41-07:00","id":909532,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/909071-exotic-airs-merit?p=909501#post909501\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not sure the Lucifuge are entirely human?</div> </div> </div> </div> They're in that liminal space I like to call &quot;abmortality&quot;; that is to say, they have blatant supernatural powers, but they're not far gone enough to not count as humans, metaphysically.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-07T16:31:10-07:00","id":909578,"title":"","content":"Don't they have an endowment that transforms them into a monsterous demonic form?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-07T16:59:57-07:00","id":909600,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/909071-exotic-airs-merit?p=909578#post909578\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Don't they have an endowment that transforms them into a monsterous demonic form?</div> </div> </div> </div>That's a singular power they can buy with their Endowment, yes. But metaphysically they are still more human than not, at least for the purposes of the rules.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-07T17:52:30-07:00","id":909643,"title":"","content":"Alright so Changeling can still harvest from the Lucifuge normally then.<br /> <br /> Would you say most minor templates are mostly mortal enough to harvest Glamour from?<br /> <br /> Like Ghouls, Wolf Blooded, Stigmatics, Proxomi, Alchemists, Heroes, Pychic Vampires, The Plain, and those with assorted Supernatural Merits, like Omen Sensitivity, or Telepathy?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-07T18:38:59-07:00","id":909689,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/909071-exotic-airs-merit?p=909643#post909643\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Alright so Changeling can still harvest from the Lucifuge normally then.<br /> <br /> Would you say most minor templates are mostly mortal enough to harvest Glamour from?<br /> <br /> Like Ghouls, Wolf Blooded, Stigmatics, Proxomi, Alchemists, Heroes, Pychic Vampires, The Plain, and those with assorted Supernatural Merits, like Omen Sensitivity, or Telepathy?</div> </div> </div> </div>In general, I'd say so long as they aren't inhuman in origin or possessing a Potence trait like Gnosis or Wyrd, they should fall under the category of harvestable.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-08T02:42:13-07:00","id":909939,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/909071-exotic-airs-merit?p=909643#post909643\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Alright so Changeling can still harvest from the Lucifuge normally then.<br /> <br /> Would you say most minor templates are mostly mortal enough to harvest Glamour from?<br /> <br /> Like Ghouls, Wolf Blooded, Stigmatics, Proxomi, Alchemists, Heroes, Pychic Vampires, The Plain, and those with assorted Supernatural Merits, like Omen Sensitivity, or Telepathy?</div> </div> </div> </div> Well some of those things aren't like the others.<br /> <br /> We don't know what alchemists are yet, since promethean second edition isn't out yet, so it's too soon to tell.<br /> <br /> As for the plain and psychic vampires, they are &quot;microtemplates,&quot; which is a themed set of supernatural merits, so they would be the same as telepaths or mediums from the core book.<br /> <br /> While time will tell, at the very least I imagine muggles with supernatural merits, even microtemplates, will be treated as human as far as changelings are concerned.<br /> <br /> In second edition werewolf, lunacy affects everyone who still has integrity instead of another &quot;morality trait,&quot; so I wouldn't be surprised if Changeling has a similar cut off point. <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}